UPDATE public.questions SET explanation = 'Technical Rationale: The end-to-end Oracle AI Vector Search Workflow follows 4 sequential stages:
1. Stage 1 (Embeddings): Chunk source documents and Generate Dense Vector Embeddings using an embedding model (via DBMS_VECTOR or external API).
2. Stage 2 (Storage): Store the generated vectors in Oracle Database tables using the native VECTOR data type.
3. Stage 3 (Indexing): Create Vector Indexes (HNSW or IVF) on the VECTOR column for fast approximate nearest neighbor search.
4. Stage 4 (Querying): Execute similarity searches using SQL functions (VECTOR_DISTANCE) combined with relational WHERE filters.
Key Exam Rule: Generating Vector Embeddings from text/data is always the foundational first step.' WHERE id = '1287dc66-1730-597d-bf48-f1412d3c57ba';
