UPDATE public.questions SET explanation = 'Technical Rationale: Oracle AI Vector Search supports distance metrics via VECTOR_DISTANCE(v1, v2, metric):
• COSINE: Measures angular separation (0 = identical orientation). Ideal for text embeddings of differing lengths.
• DOT: Inner product similarity (highest value = closest match for normalized vectors).
• EUCLIDEAN (L2): Geometric Euclidean straight-line distance between points.
• MANHATTAN (L1): Grid-based city block distance.
Key Exam Rule: COSINE measures orientation angle; EUCLIDEAN measures geometric distance.' WHERE id = 'b5fee1e7-66bd-52af-8d16-cfc27254cda4';
